From 9115192083b53562af8fc81213098b2619057b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Suresh Hemal <53757686+sureshhemal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:06:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Translate the received TOS and TTL control messages on
 macOS.

On macOS and the BSDs, a socket that enables IP_RECVTOS receives the TOS
as a control message of type IP_RECVTOS (27 on macOS) with a one-byte
payload, not as IP_TOS like on Linux. convert_control_headers() only
matched IP_TOS, so the message fell through to the "Unhandled IPPROTO_IP
message header type 27" FIXME and the application got no TOS data back.
Steam's networking sockets library asks for TOS on its UDP sockets and
asserts "No control data returned even though we asked for TOS?" on
every Steam P2P/SDR connection attempt, writing a minidump each time.

Also match IP_RECVTOS in the existing IP_TOS case, which already reads
one byte and reports WS_IP_TOS.

IP_RECVTTL has the same convention: the TTL arrives as type IP_RECVTTL
(24 on macOS) with a one-byte payload, while the existing IP_TTL case
copies four bytes, which suits Linux's int. Give IP_RECVTTL its own case
that reads one byte and reports WS_IP_TTL as an INT.

On Linux IP_RECVTOS and IP_RECVTTL are never used as control message
types, so the new cases are never reached there.

Reported and fixed in frankea/Whisky#326, where the TOS change was
verified against Steam with a patched ntdll.so. The IP_RECVTTL case was
added by Adam Franke following the reporter's note that TTL needs the
same treatment.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
index 9674d0f..71b30a5 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
@@ -432,6 +432,9 @@ static int convert_control_headers(struct msghdr *hdr, WSABUF *control)
 
 #if defined(IP_TOS)
                     case IP_TOS:
+#if defined(IP_RECVTOS) && IP_RECVTOS != IP_TOS
+                    case IP_RECVTOS: /* macOS and the BSDs report the received TOS with this type */
+#endif
                     {
                         INT tos = *(unsigned char *)CMSG_DATA(cmsg_unix);
                         ptr = fill_control_message( WS_IPPROTO_IP, WS_IP_TOS, ptr, &ctlsize,
@@ -451,6 +454,18 @@ static int convert_control_headers(struct msghdr *hdr, WSABUF *control)
                     }
 #endif /* IP_TTL */
 
+#if defined(IP_RECVTTL) && (!defined(IP_TTL) || IP_RECVTTL != IP_TTL)
+                    case IP_RECVTTL:
+                    {
+                        /* macOS and the BSDs report the received TTL with this type, as a single byte */
+                        INT ttl = *(unsigned char *)CMSG_DATA(cmsg_unix);
+                        ptr = fill_control_message( WS_IPPROTO_IP, WS_IP_TTL, ptr, &ctlsize,
+                                                    &ttl, sizeof(INT) );
+                        if (!ptr) goto error;
+                        break;
+                    }
+#endif /* IP_RECVTTL */
+
                     default:
                         FIXME("Unhandled IPPROTO_IP message header type %d\n", cmsg_unix->cmsg_type);
                         break;
-- 
